MODIFICATION NOTICE
-------------------

This is a MODIFIED version of Halcyon Video
(https://github.com/halcyon-video/halcyon-video), modified beginning
2026-09-06 by the VolkBuster Video authors.

GPL-3.0 section 5(a) requires that a modified work carry prominent notices
stating that it was changed and giving a relevant date. That is what this file
is. It is the obligation forks most often overlook, and it costs nothing to
meet.

Substantive changes from upstream:

  - Removed the 2.5D DOM store; the app is 3D only, rendered server-side.
  - Removed Jellyfin support; Plex is the only backend.
  - Removed the device gate (a viewer's browser no longer renders anything,
    so it no longer needs WebGL2).
  - Added a front door service (server/) providing Plex sign-in, an access
    gate based on Plex library sharing, signed sessions, encrypted token
    storage, and per-user configuration with owner-only enforcement.
  - Rebranded throughout.

Upstream is the origin of the 3D store itself: the procedural floor plan, the
case and poster art pipeline, the rental ritual, the clerk, the fixtures and
the period fit-out. This fork changes who the software serves and where it
renders, not what it is.


